{{Term/Store|White Goat|White Goats|Series, BotW, TotK|plural}} are recurring [[Creature]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite|'''White Goat'''|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|'''White Goat'''|Hyrule Compendium|TotK}}</ref>

==Characteristics==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|White Goat}}
White Goats are domesticated [[Goat]]s often found grazing at [[Stable]]s and in [[Hateno Pasture]]. The bells they wear are a sign of their domestication, allowing their handlers to easily find them after they have been let out to graze.<ref name="Compendium">{{Cite|These goats are raised for their multiple uses. Their milk can be drank or made into butter, and their soft fur is used to make clothes. Domesticated goats wear bells around their necks so they can be easily found after being let out to graze.|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref> White Goats are herbivorous, eating any [[Fruit]], nut, [[Vegetable]], [[Mushroom]], or [[Flower]] that they are presented with. Alongside [[Hateno Cow]]s, White Goats are kept in order to produce [[Fresh Milk]].<ref name="Compendium"/><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Fresh Milk}}<br/>This fresh milk comes from Hateno cows and white goats kept in the village. It's delicious on its own but can also be used as an ingredient in soups and stews.|Inventory|BotW}}</ref> Their Milk can be made into [[Goat Butter]], and their wool is used to make clothes.<ref name="Compendium"/><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Goat Butter}}<br/>Butter made from the milk of a domesticated white goat. In addition to being used in dishes like stews and meunière, it's often used when making cakes and other sweets.|Inventory|BotW}}</ref>

